patrone-branding (0.1.8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A new boot spinner: three interlinked rings, woven over and under like
    the Borromean rings, in Patrone's blues. A comet of light runs round
    each ring, sprinting and catching up, and the three take turns a third
    of a loop apart. 60 frames for Plymouth's 2-second loop, so a new one at
    each of its 30 ticks a second, drawn by tools/make_spinner.py. Its end
    animation, which Patrone's theme keeps off, lights the rings in full.
    Only the password prompt's images still come from Ubuntu's spinner.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:50:00 -0500

